<title>INDONESIA: Bank Niaga H1 net soars to 44.08 bln rph.</title>
<headline>Bank Niaga H1 net soars to 44.08 bln rph.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>		 (in billion rupiah unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    44.08 vs 27.95</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (in rupiah)    280 vs 484</p>
<p>    Net interest income		156.71 vs 111.41</p>
<p>    Other operating income	    40.45 vs 43.58</p>
<p>    Other operating expense	  138.24 vs 116.07</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			60.00 vs 39.25</p>
<p>Note: Bank Niaga PT said a drop in earnings per share reflected an increase in the firm's shares to 157,565,234 in 1996 from 57,777,417 in 1995 following the issuance of bonus shares and conversion of convertible bonds into shares.</p>
</text>
